  "_meta": {
    "title": "Video Retake (LTX-2.5)",
    "description": "Core ComfyUI nodes (+ KJNodes LTXVAudioVideoMask for audio regen only). Regenerates a time range of a clip with the distilled LTX-2.5 22B model and keeps everything else. The first 121 source frames (native fps) are padded to the smallest 8n+1 by holding the last frame, scaled to a /32 generation size and VAE-encoded as the init latent; SetLatentNoiseMask carries one value per latent frame (1 = regenerate, 0 = keep, fractions = partial, the strength control), so the model sees the untouched frames as clean context (per-token timesteps). 8 ManualSigmas, euler_ancestral, LTXVDualCFGGuider cfg 1. The builder (src/lib/oj/videoRetake.ts) writes the latent mask and a per-frame pixel alpha as runs of 1x1 EmptyImage batches (red channel = value) chained with ImageBatch. After decode the generation is scaled back to the source size and composited over the ORIGINAL frames with the pixel alpha: 0 outside the range (source pixels unchanged), a short ramp inside each range edge. Audio: keep (default; the source track is muxed back), follow (source audio encoded and frozen as conditioning, source track kept) or regen (source audio latent with the range masked; the decoded track replaces the source, a VAE round trip outside the range)."
